#: includes/abilities.php:204
msgid ""
"The language data on this site could not be read. This is a condition on the "
"site, not a problem with the request, so repeating the call unchanged will "
"not help; the details are in the site error log."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: comma-separated rejected keys, 2: comma-separated accepted keys.
#: includes/abilities.php:386
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Unknown input key: %1$s. This ability accepts: %2$s. A key it does not "
"declare is never read, so the request would be answered as though that key "
"had not been sent."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:388
msgid "no input at all"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:471
msgid "This ability takes no parameters. Call it with no input at all."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:820
msgid ""
"The input has to be an object, for example {\"per_page\": 50}. Both "
"parameters are optional; calling this ability with no input at all returns "
"the first page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1001
msgid ""
"WordPress locale, for example de_DE or de_DE_formal. Empty means the post "
"carries no language of its own."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1002
msgid ""
"The BCP 47 tag this locale produces in markup. de_DE and de_DE_formal both "
"produce de-DE, which is why two such versions collide in one hreflang set."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1003
msgid "Native language name, where WordPress knows one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1004
msgid ""
"Whether the language pack is installed. When it is not, the front end "
"deliberately does not switch: the page keeps the site language while its "
"meta still claims another one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1011
msgid "List the languages this site uses"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1012
msgid ""
"Returns which post types have language selection enabled, the site default "
"language, the installed language packs, and which locales published posts "
"actually carry, with counts. Call this before jpkcom-simple-lang/check-"
"translation-sets so locales and their BCP 47 tags never have to be guessed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1032
msgid ""
"Post types with language selection enabled. Everything else this plugin does "
"is scoped to these."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1033
msgid ""
"The site default language, read from WPLANG rather than from get_locale(), "
"so a temporary locale switch cannot distort it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1034
msgid ""
"Language packs installed on this site. en_US is always available and is not "
"listed here."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1037
msgid ""
"Locales that published posts carry, most used first. A locale with "
"installed=false is the case worth acting on: those posts claim a language "
"the front end cannot actually serve."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1041
msgid "Published posts carrying this locale."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1045
msgid "Published posts in the enabled post types altogether."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1046
msgid ""
"Published posts with no language of their own. This is not a gap: they are "
"served in the site default language, and hreflang reads them as that "
"language too."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1047 includes/abilities.php:1093
msgid "Locale this answer was read in."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1057
msgid "Check the translation sets for incomplete hreflang"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1058
msgid ""
"Returns the translation sets whose hreflang annotation comes out incomplete, "
"and why. The emitter keeps one entry per BCP 47 tag, so two versions "
"resolving to the same tag - two de_DE pages, or de_DE together with "
"de_DE_formal - produce a single entry and the other URL is annotated "
"nowhere. That is deliberate, because a contradictory pair would be worse, "
"but nothing in the admin says a page was dropped. This ability is what makes "
"it visible. Also reports sets with no x-default, links to unpublished or "
"deleted posts, one-way links, and members whose language pack is missing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1068
msgid "Page number, starting at 1."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1074
msgid "Sets per page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1085
msgid ""
"The site default language. A set with no version in this language gets no x-"
"default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1086
msgid ""
"How many translation sets exist altogether, so \"total\" can be read as a "
"proportion."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1087
msgid "How many of those sets have at least one finding."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1088
msgid "The page that was returned."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1089
msgid "The page size that was applied after clamping."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1090
msgid "Number of pages available."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1091
msgid ""
"True when this site has more linked posts than one call examines, so the "
"answer describes only the part that was read. Reported rather than applied "
"quietly, because an answer that stopped early while looking complete is the "
"worse failure."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1092
msgid "How many linked posts one call examines."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1096
msgid "The sets with findings, on the requested page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1100
msgid ""
"Every post ID in this set, including ones that do not appear in the output."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1101
msgid ""
"How many hreflang entries this set actually produces. Compare with the "
"number of published members: a smaller number means versions were dropped."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1104
msgid "The published members and the tag each resolves to."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1108
msgid "Post ID."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1109
msgid "Post title."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1110
msgid "Locale stored on the post, empty when it carries none."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1111
msgid ""
"True when the post carries no language of its own and is therefore read as "
"the site default - which is how a version with no language collides with an "
"explicit one in that language."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1112
msgid "The tag this version resolves to."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1118
msgid ""
"What is wrong with this set. An \"unpublished_member\" entry alone does not "
"put a set in this report - a draft translation is ordinary work in progress, "
"and flagging every one of them would make the report unreadable; it is "
"listed when the set qualifies on something else, because it explains a tag "
"count below the member count. \"tag_collision\" lists the tag and the post "
"IDs sharing it, with emitted=1 because only one of them is annotated; which "
"one survives depends on the order the posts come back in, so no winner is "
"named. \"no_x_default\" means no member carries the site default language. "
"\"unpublished_member\" and \"dangling_member\" list linked posts that never "
"appear because they are not published or no longer exist. \"one_way_link\" "
"lists members that do not link back, which the editor sync would normally "
"prevent. \"language_pack_missing\" lists members whose locale is no longer "
"installed."
msgstr ""

